A reply's reasoning ends at the first </think> token that starts a line outside a ``` fence (server/reply_text.zig).

In this tokenizer <think>/</think> are ordinary tokens (248068/248069, special false), the same ids whether the model
quotes the tag or closes its reasoning with it. Stock 1.1.7 ends the reasoning at the first close token, so a
reasoning about a chat template or a parser that quotes the tag inline (seen with pi: "outputs `<think>\n\n</think>`")
sent the rest of its reasoning to `content`, and the tool-call parser read it, so a call the reasoning only mentioned
could become a real one. Qwen 3.5 models close with "\n</think>\n\n", so the close is the first close token at a line
start outside a fence. A finished reply without one falls back to its first close token (stock); while streaming, an
inline one stays reasoning. Re-port of the ornith-1.5-122b-tensorfold recipe's 0005 onto 1.1.7's token-based split.
TENSORFOLD_THINK_LINE_CLOSE=0 restores the stock split.
A fence counts only where it opens a line (a reasoning that names a ```python block inline opens none), and a
streaming reply's search resumes past the close tokens it already rejected (no re-decoding of its prefix).
Verified: zig test -lc zig/src/server/reply_text.zig (the new cases and the stock ones); bench/think_check.py.

